{%- comment -%}
  Accessibility (2026-10-13), owner-approved micro-change 7 ("Micro-schimbări care duc Accesibilitatea la 100", phones first): many
  article bodies carry inline styles with the light pink #ea8a8a, which fails WCAG AA contrast (Lighthouse "color-contrast") as a
  text colour (2.47 on white, 2.17 on the page background, 2.05 on the pink tint boxes) and as the background of white button and
  table-header text (2.47). The bodies are live content and stay untouched: these rules override only the solid-pink colour and
  background declarations, matched on the style attribute, inside the article body. Pink tints (#ea8a8a05/08/10/15), the gradients
  and the pink borders are decorative and keep their colour.
  - pink text -> #a54f51, same hue, only darker (CIEDE2000 21.6): 4.52 on the darkest real background (the #ea8a8a15 tint over the
    page, ~#f0e8e8), 4.80 on the page background #f0f0f0, 5.47 on white.
  - pink backgrounds under white text -> #b65b5d, same hue (dE 16.0): white text 4.52.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .article-content .prose [style^="color: #ea8a8a;" i],
  .article-content .prose [style*="; color: #ea8a8a;" i] {
    color: #a54f51 !important;
  }
  .article-content .prose [style*="background: #ea8a8a;" i],
  .article-content .prose [style*="background-color: #ea8a8a;" i] {
    background-color: #b65b5d !important;
  }
</style>

